.TH SCORESTORE 2
.SH NAME
scorestore: loadint, loadreal, saveint, savereal \- persistent high scores
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "scorestore.m";
scorestore := load Scorestore Scorestore->PATH;

loadint:  fn(name: string, dflt: int):  int;
loadreal: fn(name: string, dflt: real): real;
saveint:  fn(name: string, value: int):  int;
savereal: fn(name: string, value: real): int;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Scorestore
keeps one number per
.I name
under
.BR /lib/scores ,
so that a game remembers a best score between runs.
.PP
.B Loadint
and
.B loadreal
return the stored value for
.IR name ,
or
.I dflt
if there is none or it cannot be read.
.B Saveint
and
.B savereal
write
.I value
and return 0, or \-1 if it could not be written.
.PP
A
.I name
is a single flat file name: one containing a slash, a backslash or a
NUL is rejected rather than resolved, so a caller cannot write outside
the score directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /lib/scores/ name
one file per stored score.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/scorestore.b
.SH BUGS
A failed save is reported only by the return value.
.PP
Nothing locks the file, so two programs storing the same score at once
can lose one of the values.
